1. SCOPE: WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS
================================================================================

1.1 Covered Code. Subject to Section 1.2, Covered Code means files in the
    Project that are of the following kinds:

    (a) source code written in a programming language, including (by way of
        example, not limitation) files with the extensions .cs, .c, .cc, .cpp,
        .h, .hpp, .js, .ts, .py, .java, .rs, .go, .lua, .sh, .ps1;

    (b) shader, compute-shader, and material-program source, including files
        with the extensions .shader, .compute, .cginc, .hlsl, .glsl, .shadergraph
        when expressed as program source;

    (c) build, packaging, tooling, editor-extension, test, and configuration
        files, including assembly definition files (.asmdef, .asmref), package
        manifests, project and solution configuration, continuous-integration
        configuration, and dot-files such as .gitignore;

    (d) documentation that describes the operation of the files above, where
        that documentation is written by the Licensor and does not itself
        contain Creative Assets; and

    (e) Unity sidecar metadata files (.meta) that accompany a file described in
        (a) through (d).

1.2 Files that are NOT Covered Code. The following are not Covered Code, and no
    rights in them are granted by this License:

    (a) anything within the definition of Creative Assets in Section 3.1;

    (b) serialized engine data files that embody game, level, encounter,
        narrative, visual, or animation design rather than program logic,
        including (by way of example, not limitation) Unity scene files
        (.unity), prefabs (.prefab), serialized asset files (.asset), animation
        clips (.anim), animator controllers (.controller), timeline and
        playable assets, and their accompanying .meta files; and

    (c) any file owned by a third party rather than by the Licensor (see
        Section 6).

1.3 Rule of construction. If it is unclear whether a particular file is Covered
    Code, it is NOT Covered Code for the purposes of this License, and You must
    obtain the Licensor's written permission before using it. The presence of a
    file in the same repository, directory, archive, or package as Covered Code
    does not place that file under this License.

