4. ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

4.1 Attribution in source form. If You Distribute the Covered Code or a
    Derivative Work in source form, You must retain, in that source
    distribution, a complete and unmodified copy of this License and the
    copyright notice at the top of it.

4.2 Attribution in a Product. This is the principal condition of this License.
    If You Distribute a Product, You must display the following attribution
    notice in or with that Product:

        What Lies In The Depths - Code by Drew Banyai

    The notice must appear verbatim, except that You may render the separator as
    an em dash ("What Lies In The Depths — Code by Drew Banyai") and You may add
    surrounding explanatory text such as "This product includes source code from
    the following projects:". You may not alter the project title or the
    author's name, and You may not present the notice in a way that is false or
    misleading.

    In addition to the notice, You must include a complete copy of this License,
    or a functioning link to it, in the Product's third-party notices,
    licenses screen, legal section, or accompanying documentation.

4.3 Where the notice must appear. The notice required by Section 4.2 must appear
    in at least one of the following locations within the Product:

    (a) the credits;
    (b) an acknowledgements screen or section;
    (c) an "About" screen, box, or section;
    (d) a "Licenses", "Legal", "Third-Party Notices", or "Open Source Notices"
        screen or section reachable from the Product's menus or settings; or
    (e) documentation that is distributed together with the Product, where the
        Product has no user interface capable of displaying the notice.

4.4 Minimum standard of display. In order to satisfy Section 4.2, the notice
    must meet all of the following minimum requirements. These requirements
    exist so that "attribution" has a definite meaning rather than resting on
    judgment:

    (a) it must be human-readable text, legible at the Product's normal display
        settings, and in the same script and language as the Product's other
        credits or legal notices;
    (b) it must be at least as prominent as the attribution the Product gives to
        any other third-party software component, and no less prominent than the
        smallest credit the Product gives to any individual contributor;
    (c) it must be reachable by an ordinary user of the Product through no more
        than three ordinary interactions (for example: open menu, open settings,
        open credits) from the Product's main menu, title screen, or equivalent
        entry point;
    (d) it must not be conditioned on completing the Product, achieving any
        result within it, making a purchase, creating an account, or any other
        achievement or transaction;
    (e) if the notice appears in scrolling or timed credits, the credits must be
        viewable on demand from a menu, and the notice must remain on screen
        long enough to be read; and
    (f) it must not be hidden, obscured, placed in a file that is not presented
        to the user, encrypted, or removed by any Product update.

4.5 When attribution is required, and when it is not. The obligation in
    Section 4.2 arises only when the Covered Code, or a Derivative Work of it,
    is actually incorporated into a Product that You Distribute, in any form and
    in whole or in part. It does not arise from:

    (a) running, studying, or modifying the Covered Code without Distributing a
        Product;
    (b) internal use within Your organization where no Distribution occurs;
    (c) forking or mirroring the repository (Section 4.1 applies instead); or
    (d) independent reimplementation as described in Section 2.4.

4.6 Modified versions. Modifying the Covered Code does not remove the obligation
    in Section 4.2; a Product that incorporates a modified version of the
    Covered Code must carry the notice exactly as a Product incorporating the
    unmodified version must. You may, and are encouraged to, state that the code
    has been modified. You must not remove or alter the copyright notice or this
    License text where Section 4.1 requires them to be retained.

4.7 No endorsement. The attribution notice is a statement of origin only. You
    must not use it, or any other statement, to suggest that the Licensor
    endorses, sponsors, approves, is affiliated with, or is responsible for Your
    Product or Your modifications.

